              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for inevitable, then the Russian for to arise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: несмотря на",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "несмотря на (nesmotryá na) — \"despite, in spite of\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Несмотря на дождь, мы пошли в парк. Nesmotryá na dozhd, my poshlí v park. Despite the rain, we went to the park."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes the accusative: несмотря на (nesmotryá na) погоду. Before a clause, несмотря на (nesmotryá na) то, что… — although. Несмотря is written as one word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "несмотря на (nesmotryá na) is built from не \"not\" and смотря, the gerund of смотреть \"to look\", from Proto-Slavic motriti \"to watch\": not looking at the obstacle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
