          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "тем не менее (tem ne méneye) — \"nevertheless\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Было трудно, тем не менее мы всё сделали. Býlo trúdno, tem ne méneye my vsyo sdélali. It was hard; nevertheless, we did everything."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Formal. It may open the clause or follow но: но тем не менее (tem ne méneye)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "тем не менее (tem ne méneye) is built from тем \"by that\", не \"not\" and менее \"less\", the old comparative: not the less for that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
